{"uniqueGuests doesn't actually de-duplicate the guests input and compares emails case-sensitively, allowing duplicates or case-variant blacklist bypasses to be inserted/sent downstream": 0.95807284116745, "isTeamAdminOrOwner uses && between isTeamAdmin and isTeamOwner, which requires user to be OWNER and blocks ADMIN users from adding guests": 0.9745832085609436, "sendAddGuestsEmails(evt, guests) uses the raw input rather than the filtered list that was actually added, which can misclassify new vs existing attendees and send the wrong email type": 0.9847913384437561, "In onError, message is always a non-empty string (often starting with undefined:), so the unable_to_add_guests fallback will never be used and the toast can be confusing": 0.9144579172134399, "onSuccess resets multiEmailValue but not isInvalidEmail, so reopening the dialog after a previous validation failure can immediately show the error state again": 0.8840664029121399, "MultiEmail.tsx imports primitives from @calcom/ui while living inside packages/ui, which risks circular imports now that @calcom/ui also exports MultiEmail": 0.9114462733268738}